        <p style="margin:4px 0 0;color:#444;font-size:14px;">The participle phrase always attaches to whichever noun comes right after the comma — not the noun the writer intended.</p>
        <p style="margin:6px 0 0;color:#c0392b;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;">Wrong: Walking to school, the bag fell from her shoulder.</p>
        <p style="margin:4px 0 0;color:#27ae60;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;">Correct: Walking to school, she felt her bag fall from her shoulder.</p>
