        <p style="margin:4px 0 0;color:#444;font-size:14px;">A participle phrase can dangle after a comma anywhere in a longer sentence, not just at the start.</p>
        <p style="margin:6px 0 0;color:#c0392b;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;">Wrong: The report was submitted late, having forgotten the deadline.</p>
        <p style="margin:4px 0 0;color:#27ae60;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;">Correct: Having forgotten the deadline, he submitted the report late.</p>
