<p class="pyq-question"><strong>Q1 (SSC CGL Exam Pattern):</strong> <em>Find the error: Walking through the park (a) / the flowers looked (b) / beautiful in the morning light (c) / No error (d).</em></p>
<details class="pyq-solution">
<summary>Click to view step-by-step solution &amp; rule</summary>
<div class="solution-content">
<p><strong>Answer:</strong> (a) — the sentence needs a logical subject after the comma</p>
<p><strong>Explanation:</strong> Flowers cannot "walk," so the participle phrase dangles. Correct: "Walking through the park, I found the flowers beautiful in the morning light."</p>
</div>
</details>
</div>

<div class="pyq-card">
<p class="pyq-question"><strong>Q2 (Bank PO Exam Pattern):</strong> <em>Having completed the project, the client was informed by the team.</em> (Spot and correct the error)</p>
<details class="pyq-solution">
<summary>Click to view step-by-step solution &amp; rule</summary>
<div class="solution-content">
<p><strong>Answer:</strong> Rewrite as: "Having completed the project, the team informed the client."</p>
<p><strong>Explanation:</strong> The client didn't complete the project — the team did. The subject right after the comma must be the one performing the participle's action.</p>
</div>
</details>
